# A closed hat, one node: six square partials from 205 Hz that share no
# harmonic, a fifth of it noise, in a band at 9 kHz and cut under 7. Measured:
# 20 dB down at 13 ms, 40 at 30, over (60 dB down) at 45 ms on a note of any
# length; loudest at 8.8 kHz; the node peaks at 0.43 of full scale. decay= is
# its length: 320ms is the same hat open. Not tuned to the note. 3 dB quieter
# on an engine built at 32 kHz, 6 at 22.05.
instrument tick {
  hat(decay=45ms, band=9000hz, floor=7000hz, noise=0.2) as h
  h > out
}
